    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output tonight, led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) and **Junior Caminero** (76.88). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier play, benefiting from a favorable matchup against McGreevy, where his elite sprint speed and leadoff placement create the highest raw ceiling in our lineup. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** occupies the #3 spot and is primed to exploit a 5.02 xERA matchup against Quantrill. **Trea Turner** (68.96) remains an essential catalyst; while he faces Alcantara, his BvP history and leadoff efficiency secure his status as a lock in the lineup.\n\nOur strategy heavily weights speed and platoon optimization. **Lars Nootbaar** (63.66) and **Christian Yelich** (62.06) both benefit from strong platoon advantages that elevated their projections well into the recommended range. Conversely, **Yordan Alvarez** (56.32) presents a calculated risk; despite his elite xwOBA, the L/L platoon disadvantage against Detmers pulls his efficiency score below our typical \"Strong\" threshold. In terms of bench decisions, **Dillon Dingler** (39.01) was the closest to cracking the starting nine. Ultimately, he fell just short of our 40.0 floor due to a poor platoon setup against Kremer, reinforcing our disciplined approach to preserving game caps. \n\nManagement is monitoring the lineup integrity of our utility options as we push for volume in the SB category. **Caleb Durbin** (56.66) is included for his late-game stolen base potential despite a tougher matchup against Jump. We are cautiously navigating risks regarding potential weather delays or mid-game substitutions for **Josh Smith**, who sits at 45.71 and remains on a short leash. While **Kyle Schwarber** and **Hyeseong Kim** remain unavailable, the depth provided by our active roster\u2014including **Colt Keith** and **Jacob Gonzalez**\u2014should provide enough categorical stability to maintain our standing in the league.",
